The total number of holes is calculated by multiplying the number of two-hole buttons by the holes per button and adding the result to the number of four-hole buttons. 

\[
7 \text{ buttons} \times 2 \text{ holes/button} = 14 \text{ holes}
\]
\[
14 \text{ buttons} \times 4 \text{ holes/button} = 56 \text{ holes}
\]
\[
14 \text{ holes} + 56 \text{ holes} = 70 \text{ holes}
\]

\boxed{70}

